# --- Local storage and logs --------------------------------------------------
#
# These are **anchored with a leading slash** so they match only the directory at the
# repository root, which is the one they are about.
#
# An unanchored `storage/` matches a directory of that name at *any* depth, and it did:
# it silently excluded `src/bm/infra/storage/`, the object-store module that
# `bm.api.v1.imports` and `bm.domain.imports.service` both import. The module was never
# pushed, so a fresh clone of this repository could not import its own imports API
# (`ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'bm.infra.storage'`), `mypy src/` reported two
# errors, and `pytest` could not even collect `tests/unit/test_upload_storage.py`.
# Nothing in the working tree showed it — `git status` was clean, because an ignored file
# is not untracked-and-reported, it is invisible.
#
# The same trap applies to each of the others, so all four are anchored rather than only
# the one that had already sprung.
*.log
/logs/
/storage/
/uploads/
*.sqlite3
*.db

# --- Editor and OS -----------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
